This product includes original code (core/inference/mtp/) implementing
Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) self-speculative decoding for Qwen3.5/3.6 models.
That code is Mira's own and is released under Mira's MIT License (see LICENSE).

The MTP mechanism was studied from the following works. No source code from
them is copied into this repository; they are acknowledged here because ideas
and conventions were learned from them:

  - oMLX (https://github.com/jundot/omlx)
    Copyright (c) jundot
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    Its patches/mlx_lm_mtp/ layer is a monkey-patch of mlx-lm that adds MTP
    support. Reading it clarified how an MTP head attaches to mlx-lm's Qwen3.5
    model and, in particular, the RMSNorm weight-shift ("+1") convention that
    the sidecar sanitize step must apply or draft acceptance collapses. A copy
    of the Apache-2.0 license text is available at:
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

  - mlx-lm PR #990 (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm/pull/990)
    Copyright (c) Apple Inc.
    Licensed under the MIT License.
    Proposes native Qwen3.5/3.6 MTP support in mlx-lm; used as a reference for
    the head module and sidecar layout.

  - DeepSeek-V3 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.19437) and Qwen3, for the MTP head
    design and the draft/verify decoding scheme.
